@@AUDIT@@

Equation~\eqref{eq:loop-shared-result} supports arbitrary positive \(L\)
within this scalar family, and the finite tests check the stated loop
orders. Generic multiloop scattering families have additional independent
scalar products, numerator powers and kinematic variables. Their equation
structure requires separate validation. The present timing gains therefore
apply to the specified coupled vacuum family and supplied-identity
workflow~\cite{KiraHigherLoopData}.
